Per-settle Ir = (Ir@201 - Ir@1) / 200; 50 effects parked per settle.

  baseline       (255,009,385 -   171,341,182) / 200 =    418,341    1.00x
  nosort           (352,006,722 - 172,223,399) / 200 =    898,917    2.15x
  fast             (619,298,528 - 173,722,118) / 200 =  2,227,882    5.33x
  popped-scrub   (2,954,511,267 - 187,067,233) / 200 = 13,837,220   33.07x

`nosort` is `fast` without the ascending-id order, so the SORT's share is
2,227,882 - 898,917 = 1,328,965 Ir (60% of door 2's measured cost) and the
PHASE SPLIT's is 898,917 - 418,341 = 480,576 Ir (~9,600 per parked effect).

`popped-scrub` reads and rewrites the whole `Shared<List>` per park and per
pop — O(k^2) ELEMENT COPIES per settle. It is recorded to name the trap, not
as door 2's cost.
